  "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. Running it confirms this.\n\n1. `service2.py` imports only `pricing.base_fee` and `discounts.apply_discount`.\n2. `base_fee(1000)` = 500 + 1000 // 10 = **600**\n3. `apply_discount(600, \"gold\")`: gold is 20%, so 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 600 \u2212 120 = **480**\n\nNothing imports `decoy_tax.py` or `decoy_shipping.py`, so they don't change the result.\n\nANSWER: 480",
